  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Viviendo con Felinos: Community and Conservation Living with Felines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to extend protections for jaguars and other felines on ranches surrounding the 55,000-acre Northern Jaguar Reserve in Sahuaripa, Sonora. Living with Jaguars works closely with ranchers to minimize human-wildlife conflicts, poaching, and restore essential wildlife habitat for the areas four large felines jaguar, ocelot, mountain lion, and bobcat. Project activities include: 1) assist ranchers with restoration, water conservation, and water sanitation projects; 2) engage local youth in activities that connect them with nature; 3) training a local wildlands firefighting crew and helping create a position for a livestock depredation insurance inspector; 4) increase local involvement by teaching vaqueros camera maintenance; 5) train volunteers on how to monitor wildlife corridors along Mexico Highway 2; 6) establish an environmental monitoring committee in conjunction with PROCODES, and 7) achieve the official designation of the Northern Jaguar Reserve as a Flora and Fauna Protected Area.</narrative>
  </description>
